\subsection{Benchmark Evaluation Dataset}
Evaluation was performed on the official \textbf{DocVQA} validation set \cite{b1}. We sampled 200 diverse document-question pairs (Experiment ID: \texttt{EXP-0002}, Seed $0$) spanning varied document archetypes: forms, financial tables, multi-column reports, typed correspondence, historical archives, handwritten notes, and technical diagrams.

\subsection{Evaluation Metrics}
Following established DocVQA standards, we evaluate:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{Exact Match (EM):} Percentage of predictions matching at least one ground-truth gold annotation exactly after casing and punctuation normalization:
    \begin{equation}
        \text{EM} = \frac{1}{N} \sum_{i=1}^N \max_{g \in \mathcal{G}_i} \mathbb{I}(\text{norm}(p_i) = \text{norm}(g))
        \label{eq:em}
    \end{equation}
    \item \textbf{Average Normalized Levenshtein Similarity (ANLS):} Soft similarity metric with a threshold $\tau = 0.5$ \cite{b2}:
    \begin{equation}
        \text{ANLS} = \frac{1}{N} \sum_{i=1}^N \max_{g \in \mathcal{G}_i} s(p_i, g)
        \label{eq:anls}
    \end{equation}
    where $s(p, g) = 1 - \frac{\text{Lev}(p, g)}{\max(|p|, |g|)}$ if $\frac{\text{Lev}(p, g)}{\max(|p|, |g|)} < 0.5$, else $0.0$.
    \item \textbf{Contains Match:} Proportion of predictions where the gold answer string is fully contained within the predicted output.
    \item \textbf{OCR Answer Coverage Ceiling:} Proportion of evaluation items where at least one ground-truth gold answer is verbatim present within the raw OCR extracted text.
    \item \textbf{Paired Statistical Significance:} 95\% percentile bootstrap confidence intervals ($B = 1000$ iterations) for ANLS differences, and McNemar's paired test for binary EM outcomes.
\end{enumerate}

